{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Choosing a storage","modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Pick the sparse-set or the archetype storage for a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","isActive":true},{"text":", and know what changes.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps its entities and components in one of two storages, chosen when it is created:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let nexus = Nexus()                       \/\/ the default, same as Nexus(storage: .archetype)","let churning = Nexus(storage: .sparseSet) \/\/ for heavy add\/remove churn"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both storages offer the same API with the same observable behavior: generational entity identifiers, events, the structural lock and its traps, families, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading:writing:)"},{"type":"text","text":", spans, snapshots, cloning and the entity state machine. Every test of the package runs against both. What differs is where the components live in memory, and with it what is cheap."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/default"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype"},{"type":"text","text":", so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Nexus()"},{"type":"text","text":" uses it. Choose "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet"},{"type":"text","text":" explicitly for workloads dominated by heavy component add and remove churn (see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick"},{"type":"text","text":"). There is no storage protocol: the set of storages is closed, and a nexus switches on its storage once per call, so each storage compiles to concrete code."}]},{"text":"The sparse-set storage","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"The-sparse-set-storage"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps one dense array per component type, a paged sparse index per type that maps an entity to its slot in that array, and a bitset of component types per entity. Adding or removing a component touches the data of that one type only, and no other component moves. Looking up one component is a sparse index read plus an array read."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating a family is the weak spot: the members of a family are stored in each component array in the order the components were added, so every extra component type costs a lookup per member, and the reads are scattered once the arrays were shuffled by churn."}]},{"text":"The archetype storage","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"The-archetype-storage"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype"},{"type":"text","text":" follows the design of "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html"},{"type":"text","text":": entities with exactly the same component types live in one table, with a column (an array) per component type. An index maps every entity to its table and row. Tables are created when a component set appears first, and adding or removing one component type moves the entity’s row to another table along a cached edge of the table graph."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating a family visits the tables that match it, and walks their columns linearly: no lookup per member and a sequential read per component. The list of matching tables is cached per family, which the nexus lists when the family is created and extends when a new table appears. A table that became empty stays alive, along with its columns and its entry in the cached lists, where an iteration skips it. Cleaning the nexus with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()"},{"type":"text","text":" drops all tables."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In flecs this is the default, and sparse components are the opt-in trait ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sparse"},{"type":"text","text":"): “Sparse components are stored outside of tables, which means they do not have to be moved”, trading query speed for component add and remove speed (see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md"},{"type":"text","text":"). Fireblade 1.x was the reverse, a sparse set per component type; the two storages make that a choice per nexus instead of per component."}]},{"text":"What the numbers say","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"What-the-numbers-say"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Measured with 10 000 entities, release build, Apple silicon, wall clock p50 per pass ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"make benchmark"},{"type":"text","text":", see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Benchmarks\/"},{"type":"text","text":"):"}]},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Case","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Sparse set","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Archetype","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"11 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2.5 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A, B)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"18 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"4.3 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A, B, C, D)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"31 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"7.7 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A, writing: B)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"17 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"4.4 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A, B, writing: C)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"23 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"6.1 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2 reads, 10% of the entities match","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"3.6 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"1.3 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2 reads, 100 000 entities with shuffled storage order","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"227 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"27 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2 reads, 1 024 different component sets","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"18 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"11 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Parameter pack, 5 reads and 2 writes","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2 200 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"1 800 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Plain ","type":"text"},{"code":"for","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over a family, 2 components","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"455 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"455 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Random ","type":"text"},{"code":"entity.get","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of one component, 10 000 lookups","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"334 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"345 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add a component to each entity and remove it again, 10 000 entities","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2 180 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"4 900 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Create and destroy 1 000 entities with 7 components","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"1 730 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2 510 μs","type":"text"}]}]]],"alignments":["left","right","right"],"type":"table"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Fireblade 1.x needed 480 μs for the plain iteration of one component and 1 220 μs for two ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IterOnlyOneComponent"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IterOnlyTwoComponents"},{"type":"text","text":"). Both storages iterate without any allocation."}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Iterating with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading:writing:)"},{"text":" is 1.6 to 8 times faster on the archetype storage: about 4 times in the plain case, 8 times when the sparse-set arrays are shuffled against each other, and least when the entities are spread over many small tables.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Changing the component set of an entity costs about twice as much on the archetype storage: the whole row moves. An entity that changes its component set less than once in a few frames is far ahead on iteration; a world that toggles a component on most entities every frame is better off with the sparse set.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Plain ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"text":" iteration and random access cost the same on both: they look every component up per entity.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Entity creation and destruction are a bit slower on the archetype storage, because the row of every component moves with the entity.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"Which storage to pick","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Which-storage-to-pick"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default is the archetype storage: it iterates faster (see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say"},{"type":"text","text":"), and iteration is what most worlds spend their time on."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off: the archetype storage buys iteration speed with the cost of moving a row whenever the component set of an entity changes. Prefer "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet"},{"type":"text","text":" when the workload is dominated by heavy add and remove churn, for example toggling a component on most entities every frame. This matches flecs, where sparse components are the opt-in trait for components that are added and removed often."}]},{"text":"Differences you can observe","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Differences-you-can-observe"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Iteration order.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The sparse-set storage visits the members of a family in the order of the family’s member list, the archetype storage table by table and row by row, and rows move when entities change tables. Neither order is a contract; use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity\/identifier"},{"text":" or your own key if you need one.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Single-type spans.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(writing:_:)"},{"text":" view one contiguous array. On the archetype storage a type is stored in one column per table, so if entities with different component sets have the type, the span views a temporary copy made table by table (and the writing variant stores it back when the closure returns, also when it throws). That costs one allocation and a copy per call, and nothing can observe the difference while the closure runs, because the type is locked.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Family spans.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Family\/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)"},{"text":" passes one batch per matching table on the archetype storage, however the nexus was used before; the sparse-set storage passes shorter batches after churn. Both visit every member exactly once, and the closure must be correct for any batch size.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents"},{"type":"text","text":" for the spans."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Benchmarks":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks","role":"article","title":"Benchmarks","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/benchmarks","abstract":[{"text":"See how FirebladeECS revisions compare on a shared workload suite, and run the comparison yourself.","type":"text"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind/archetype":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"archetype","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Nexus.StorageKind.archetype","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind\/archetype","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One table per component set, a column per component type in every table, an index from entity to table and row."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEvent":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEvent"}],"title":"NexusEvent","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexusevent","abstract":[{"text":"A marker protocol for all Nexus events.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEvent"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEventMask":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexuseventmask","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The kinds of events a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate"},{"text":" subscribes to.","type":"text"}],"title":"NexusEventMask","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NexusEventMask","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NexusEventMask","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/init(storage:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/init(storage:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"storage","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Nexus","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"StorageKind","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC11StorageKindO"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"title":"init(storage:)","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/init(storage:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Initializes a new Nexus."}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/clear()":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/clear()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Clears all data from the Nexus."}],"title":"clear()","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"clear"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}]},"https://github.com/SanderMertens/flecs/blob/master/docs/ComponentTraits.md":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"component traits"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md","title":"component traits","type":"link"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A lightweight, fast and easy to use Entity-Component System in Swift."}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS","title":"FirebladeECS","role":"collection"},"https://www.flecs.dev/flecs/md_docs_2Queries.html":{"url":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"flecs"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html","title":"flecs","type":"link"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/componentSpan(reading:_:)":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"componentSpan"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Result"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"reading"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":".Type, ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Span","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4SpanV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":">) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Result"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"rethrows"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Result"}],"title":"componentSpan(reading:_:)","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/componentspan(reading:_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Gives ","type":"text"},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" read access to all components of a type as one contiguous ","type":"text"},{"code":"Span","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind/default":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"`default`","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Nexus","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"StorageKind","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC11StorageKindO"}],"title":"default","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind\/default","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/default","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The storage "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/init(storage:)"},{"type":"text","text":" uses by default: "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/MigratingToFirebladeECS2":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/migratingtofirebladeecs2","abstract":[{"text":"Move a project from FirebladeECS 1.x to 2.0: components become value types, and every write goes through the nexus.","type":"text"}],"title":"Migrating to FirebladeECS 2","type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind/sparseSet":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sparseSet","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Nexus.StorageKind.sparseSet","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind\/sparseset","abstract":[{"type":"text","text